@startuml
!theme plain
|a_default| Default
|a_default|
start
:the process begins;
:receiving the invoice;
:it is sorted per client;
:it is then sorted per vendor;
:attach the invoice entry form to the invoice;
:the required information is entered onto the form;
:the completeness of the invoice is checked;
:v1: check completeness of invoice ({Complete, Incomplete}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v1 = "Incomplete"])
:If the invoice is not complete;
:the process ends;
stop
else ([v1 = "Complete"])
:the information for the SLA is entered. The date for completion is also entered and the priority is checked.;
:the priority is checked;
:v2: check priority level ({High, Low}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v2 = "High"])
:If the priority is high;
:a red stamp is placed on the entry invoice;
else ([v2 = "Low"])
->;
endif
repeat :;
:The invoice compliance is then checked;
:v3: check compliance status ({Complete, Incomplete}); <<objectSignal>>
backward:If it is not complete, the check continues.;
repeat while () is ([v3 = "Incomplete"]) not ([v3 = "Complete"])
:If it is complete, the process continues.;
:v4: case type ({Experienced, Normal, Other}); <<objectSignal>>
switch ()
case ([v4 = "Experienced"])
:If the invoice needs to be sent to experienced staff;
:the non-compliance invoice is processed;
:Finally, the client is called and information is requested.;
:The invoice is then batched and allocated to DEO;
:and the process ends;
stop
case ([v4 = "Normal"])
:the client is called;
case ([v4 = "Other"])
:a postal mail is sent requesting complete information and the process ends.;
stop
endswitch
endif
@enduml